      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, about double the maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin (2,550 mg/day, and many protocols cap it lower). Metformin also doesn't come in a 1700 mg tablet, so the intended dose may be a transcription error, such as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg three times daily.\n\nMedication orders also need to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the clinical decision. Please have the treating physician review and enter the order directly, or confirm the intended dose with them. If you tell me the prescriber's intended dose and the formulation, I can help you check it against standard limits, but I'd still recommend the prescriber enter it."
      }
